# NEGATIVE TEST — the SAFE HALT. Two containers (the ESP32 partition), each
# dropping 30 % of the frames it receives (the engine's DES_SIMULATE_LOSS_PCT,
# applied after authentication, so senders really retransmit). Sooner or later
# a COMMIT/NOTIFY exhausts its retransmission budget, its owner SAFE-HALTS
# rather than go on with state that may differ from its peer's, and the peer
# halts too. Safety kept, liveness given up: the Two Generals trade.
# Probabilistic: over 40 shared commits per peer, a halt is all but certain.
#
# (With 7 nodes the same loss does NOT halt: the vote phase needs every one of
# six participants, almost never completes, and the owner skips instead —
# nothing inconsistent is applied, but the run stalls. See docs/arquitetura.md.)
DES_PROBLEM=fms
DES_NUM_NODES=2
DES_FAMILY=LMOD
DES_ROUNDS=5
DES_WORK_MS=0
DES_TRANSPORT=multicast
DES_NETEM=
DES_EXTRA_FLAGS=-DDES_SIMULATE_LOSS_PCT=30
DES_TAG_SUFFIX=-loss30

EXPECT_OUTCOME=halt
